{"author":"RebarBotNava","author_email":"joeoakhart+bot@navapbc.com","author_id":"594c-9dcf-5ad6-4e6d","author_sig":"{\"payload\": \"\", \"payloadType\": \"application/vnd.rebar.authorship.v1+json\", \"signatures\": [{\"keyid\": \"594c-9dcf-5ad6-4e6d\", \"sig\": \"\"}]}","data":{"content_hash":"87eae90fb7cd26a5ddbf29f2e75d5bf43a69606e319c8baef047d6cee03704b9","digest":{"component_or_area":"infra/scripts/observability.sh","key_entities":["infra/scripts/observability.sh","aws cloudwatch put-metric-data","replication","voter","merge-change","deploy","G2P","shared deferral/interrupt helper","offset file","tests/scripts/test_observability_offsets_6a65.py","tests/scripts/test_observability_exit.py"],"problem_keywords":["cumulative counter","offset acknowledgement","CloudWatch publish","transient failure","metric loss","observability"],"propositions":["Cumulative error counter streams in observability.sh persist offset before CloudWatch put-metric-data succeeds, so a transient AWS failure causes the next interval to compute zero delta and permanently lose the failed count.","Seven metric streams across six code shapes (replication, voter, merge-change, deploy, two shared helper metrics, G2P) share the same pre-acknowledgement defect.","Offset must advance only after successful AWS publication; on failure the offset remains byte-identical so retry computes and publishes the accumulated delta.","Regression test proves each stream leaves offset unchanged after forced AWS failure, republishes the accumulated delta on successful retry, then advances offset only after success."]},"digest_hash_version":1,"model":"bedrock:us.anthropic.claude-opus-4-8","schema":"ticket_digest_v1"},"env_id":"b8a354e0-12c3-4cf2-bbf1-fcc9685d5126","event_type":"TICKET_DIGEST","timestamp":1787909611853033001,"uuid":"2806f992-7606-48ea-b815-f3ac217060a8"}